  "content": {
    "title": "When does 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' come out? Trailer drops tomorrow",
    "text": "March 17, 2026, 11:47 a.m. ETThe first trailer for \"Spider-Man: Brand New Day\" is set to be released on March 18, 2026.Tom Holland, Zendaya, and Jacob Batalon will reprise their roles in the new film.The plot follows Peter Parker after the events of \"No Way Home,\" where no one remembers who he is.Marvel fans, are your \"spidey senses\" tingling?The first trailer for \"Spider-Man: Brand New Day\" drops tomorrow, with multiple two-second teaser posts scattered on social media ahead of the release.Tom Holland took to Instagram on Tuesday to share that Marvel is \"doing something that has never been done before,\" adding that \"some of our greatest fans are going to help us release pieces\" of the trailer. Multiple fan accounts across the globe have been posting these clips, from Ohio to Peru.It is unknown exactly when the trailer will drop, only that it will be posted sometime in the morning on March 18, according to Holland. But when does the movie actually come out?When does 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' come out?\"Spider-Man: Brand New Day\" comes out on Friday, July 31, 2026.As of March 2026, tickets to \"Spider-Man: Brand New Brand\" have not been released.See 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' 2026 castTom Holland as Peter Parker/Spider-ManZendaya as Michelle \"MJ\" Jones-WatsonJacob Batalon as Ned LeedsJon Bernthal as Frank Castle/PunisherMark Ruffalo as Bruce Banner/HulkMichael Mando as Mac Gargan/ScorpionMarvin Jones III as Lonnie Lincoln/TombstoneThe cast also includes \"Stranger Things\" actress, \"Severance\" actor Tramell Tillman and \"The Bear\" actress Liza Colón-Zayas in unknown roles.What will happen in 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day'?\"Spider-Man: Brand New Day\" follows Peter Parker after the ending of 2021's \"Spider-Man: No Way Home,\" where the entire world loses all memory of Parker, including his girlfriend MJ (Zendaya) and best friend Ned (Jacob Batalon).The newest Spider-Man flick shows Parker ditching the superhero suit to focus on college, but \"when a new threat endangers his friends, he must break his promise and suit up again, teaming with an unexpected ally to protect those he loves.\"Are the 'Spider-Man' movies on Disney+? Where to stream themFans of the Marvel movies might notice that Holland's first three Spider-Man flicks take a while to head to Disney+. Sony Pictures owns the film distribution rights to the character, not Disney. They have had separate licensing deals with streaming services.So, where can you stream them? Here's where to find them:Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017): Disney+, fuboTV, Amazon Prime, Peacock Premium, YouTube TVSpider-Man: Far From Home (2019): Disney+, fuboTV, YouTube TVSpider-Man: No Way Home (2021): Philo, StarzWatch 'Spider-Man' films on Disney+The movies are also available to buy or rent on Apple TV and Amazon Prime Video.Samantha Neely is a trending reporter for the USA TODAY NETWORK-Florida, covering pop culture, theme parks, breaking news and more. You can get all of Florida’s best content directly in your inbox each weekday by signing up for the free newsletter, Florida TODAY, at https://floridatoday.com/newsletters.",
